\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Comparing the geometry of multiplicative Yang-Mills connections (YM conn.) with the geometry of singular foliations. Here, $\mathscr  {F}$-connections only serve to highlight a geometric interpretation, but we actually provided a notion only defined as associated to $P$; however, the general notion of $\mathscr  {F}$-connections allows for more than such connections if $H$ is not simple; this will not matter here, see\nonbreakingspace \cite  {Fischer:2401.05966} for the general classification of $\mathscr  {F}$-connections and their relation to multiplicative Yang-Mills connections.}}{116}{table.342}\protected@file@percent }
